  "description": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Saint Mary's College of California is a private Catholic, Lasallian liberal arts college in Moraga, California, in the San Francisco Bay Area. Founded in 1863 by Archbishop Joseph Alemany and transferred to the De La Salle Brothers in 1868, the college relocated to its current 420-acre Moraga campus in 1928. It is the only California institution and the only Catholic institution included in the Loren Pope book Colleges That Change Lives.",
      "Saint Mary's organises its academic life around four schools — the School of Liberal Arts, the School of Science, the School of Economics and Business Administration, and the Kalmanovitz School of Education — offering roughly 40 undergraduate majors and 36 graduate and professional studies programs. The signature Collegiate Seminar and the Integral Curriculum of Liberal Arts (Great Books) anchor a strong liberal-arts core across every degree.",
      "The college follows a distinctive 4-1-4 academic calendar: a fall semester, a four-week immersive January Term, and a spring semester. Class sizes are small (average 19 students, 10:1–13:1 student-faculty ratio), and the campus blends California Churrigueresque and Spanish Colonial Revival architecture across the Moraga hills, with all first-year students living in residence.",
      "Saint Mary's is part of the NCAA Division I West Coast Conference as the Gaels and is known for its Australian basketball recruiting pipeline. International students enter through standard undergraduate or graduate admissions; the college reports Princeton Review Top 391, U.S. News Regional #4 (West), and Top 5% earning potential (Payscale 2024) among its distinctives."
    ],
    "paragraphsRu": [
      "Saint Mary's College of California — частный католический Lasallian liberal arts college в городе Moraga, Калифорния, в San Francisco Bay Area. Основан в 1863 году архиепископом Joseph Alemany, в 1868 передан De La Salle Brothers, в 1928 переехал на нынешний 420-акровый кампус в Moraga. Единственный калифорнийский и единственный католический колледж в книге Loren Pope «Colleges That Change Lives».",
      "Академическая жизнь Saint Mary's организована вокруг четырёх школ — School of Liberal Arts, School of Science, School of Economics and Business Administration, Kalmanovitz School of Education — около 40 бакалаврских специальностей и 36 graduate / professional studies программ. Фирменный Collegiate Seminar и Integral Curriculum of Liberal Arts (Great Books) формируют сильное liberal-arts ядро во всех степенях.",
      "Колледж работает по особому календарю 4-1-4: осенний семестр, четырёхнедельный погружённый January Term и весенний семестр. Маленькие классы (в среднем 19 студентов, соотношение студент/преподаватель 10:1–13:1), а кампус сочетает California Churrigueresque и Spanish Colonial Revival архитектуру в холмах Moraga — все first-year students живут на кампусе.",
      "Saint Mary's играет в NCAA Division I West Coast Conference под прозвищем Gaels и известен своим австралийским баскетбольным recruiting pipeline. Международные студенты поступают через стандартный undergraduate / graduate admissions; среди отличий — Princeton Review Top 391, U.S. News Regional #4 (West) и Top 5% по earning potential (Payscale 2024)."
    ],
    "keyFacts": [
      "Founded 1863 — California's second-oldest college",
      "Catholic Lasallian — De La Salle Brothers tradition",
      "420-acre campus in Moraga, San Francisco Bay Area",
